# Nutmeg Project Standards

- Be concise in all responses.
- Prefer short answers.
- Avoid repetition.
- Use bullet points instead of long paragraphs.
- Do not explain obvious concepts.
- Do not repeat the question when prompted.
- Keep changes focused and minimal; avoid broad refactors unless requested.
- Do not break existing API contracts between `flutter/` and `backend/`.
- Reuse existing UI components and styles (`Palette`, `TextPalette`, shared widgets) before creating new ones.
- Any user-facing text must be localized via `flutter/lib/l10n/*.arb` and regenerated with `flutter gen-l10n`.
- Preserve current behavior unless the task explicitly asks for a behavior change.

## Flutter/Dart

- Follow existing screen patterns (`Section`, `PageTemplate`, form validation).
- Prefer null-safe, straightforward state updates; avoid introducing unnecessary abstractions.
- For visual changes, keep responsive layout behavior consistent with existing screens.

## Backend/Python

- Keep blueprint endpoints and payload shapes backward compatible.
- Validate inputs and return clear HTTP status codes for failures.
- Reuse shared utilities and avoid duplicate logic across blueprints.

## Verification

- After edits, run a quick lint/diagnostic check on touched files.
- If localization keys are added or changed, regenerate localization outputs.
